        "fov_deg": 55.0,
        "_moved_to_the_town_2026_08_26": "WAS (354600, -321400, 30000) facing yaw 135 -- a clearing 8,245 m from the town, trace-placed in 2026-08-15 to make the kilometre walk test possible. That was INSTRUMENT SCAFFOLDING, never a design decision: nobody ruled that the game begins in that forest. It is now the TOWN PLAZA. WORLD_VISION already decided this at the landform level -- the basins are where people live and the foothill-to-peak arc is distance from safety -- so a player starting 8 km out begins at the WRONG END of the remoteness gradient and the world's difficulty reading is inverted from the first minute. This camera's rotation_deg governs CAPTURE ONLY -- place_player_start takes the actor's facing as its own --yaw argument and does NOT read it from here, so the spawn was placed with --yaw 35 to face the landmark tower across the plaza. Stated because the first run silently used the tool's default 135 and a comment claiming otherwise would have been false the moment it was written. ONE start, not two: UE picks among multiple PlayerStarts unpredictably, and a spawn that depends on engine enumeration order is exactly the silent variable this project exists to kill. The old coordinates survive here and in git; the walk-test tooling spawns pawns anywhere and never needed the actor."
